'''''Allium longispathum''''', or the '''Mediterranean onion''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Amaryllidaceae]], native to [[Macaronesia]] and the Mediterranean basin.<ref name="528340-1">{{cite POWO |id=528340-1 |title=''Allium longispathum'' Redouté |access-date=31 March 2022 }}</ref><ref name="commonname">{{cite web |url=https://identify.plantnet.org/weurope/species/Allium%20longispathum%20D.Delaroche/data |title=''Allium longispathum'' D.Delaroche |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2022 |website=plantnet.org |publisher=Pl@ntNet |access-date=31 March 2022 }}</ref> Some authorities consider it a subspecies of pale garlic, ''[[Allium paniculatum]]''.<ref name="GBIF_8366402">{{cite web |title=''Allium longispathum'' Redouté |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/8366402 |website=gbif.org |publisher=GBIF Secretariat |author=GBIF Backbone Taxonomy |access-date=31 March 2022 }}</ref>

